<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ixhjtwi"><img id="fkt-image-ce3-486-893" title="" target="_self" src="{{ 'shila-1.webp' | asset_url }}" href="" align="center" alt="" width="1200" height="675" onclick="" class="fk-image-defaults" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div>

<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ih8f78">
<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-ASKCcEx7Klw3"><b>Dear Friend Worried About Aging,</b><br><br>If you're reading this with that quiet, creeping suspicion that something has shifted in your body over the last few years — the stiffness when you stand up, the afternoon fog that didn't used to be there, the face in the mirror that looks like it's settling in instead of still building — I want you to stop scrolling for a moment.<br><br>I almost didn't write this letter.<br><br>As a longevity doctor with twenty-six years in translational biology, I am careful about what I put my name to.<br><br>But what I have watched happen in my own clinic over the last fourteen months, in the bloodwork of patients I have personally followed back from Shanghai, is something I cannot in good conscience keep quiet about.<br><br>So I'm going to tell you what I saw, what it means, and exactly what to do with this information — if you have the courage to actually act on it.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i5sihc">THE PHONE CALL THAT CHANGED EVERYTHING I THOUGHT I KNEW ABOUT AGING…</div>

<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="itcqk86"><img id="fkt-image-8f3-da0-9f5" title="" target="_self" src="{{ 'shila-2.webp' | asset_url }}" href="" align="center" alt="" width="" height="" onclick="" class="fk-image-defaults disable-fk-lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i2700n">It happened on a Tuesday afternoon. I had just finished rounds when my phone rang.<br><br>It was James Calloway — a longtime patient, sixty-four years old, retired managing partner of one of the largest private equity firms in the Northeast. James is the kind of man who plays squash four mornings a week, reads three medical journals for fun, and has never once missed his annual executive physical. He is also the kind of man who does not call his doctor in the middle of the day unless something is wrong.<br><br><blockquote style="border-left:4px solid #c1272d; padding:8px 12px; margin:14px 0; font-style:italic; background:#faf7f2">"Marcus," he said, "I need you to look at my numbers. I just got back from Shanghai."</blockquote>I almost laughed. "James, why on Earth were you in Shanghai?"<br><br><blockquote style="border-left:4px solid #c1272d; padding:8px 12px; margin:14px 0; font-style:italic; background:#faf7f2">"Because two of my partners have been going for the last eight months. And Marcus — they don't look the same anymore. I'm not talking about a tan. I'm talking about the way their skin sits on their face. The way they get out of a chair. Last weekend I watched Bill — he's sixty-eight — beat his thirty-five-year-old son in straight sets. I have known Bill for twenty-two years. The man couldn't climb a flight of stairs without complaining about his knee last year."</blockquote>That was the call.<br><br>A week later, James was sitting in my office sliding a manila envelope across my desk. Inside was a TruDiagnostic epigenetic panel — baseline, and again ninety days later.<br><br><b>His biological age had dropped from 71.2 to 34.6.</b><br><br>Thirty-six and a half years. In ninety days.<br><br>I have been doing this for a long time. I have never seen numbers like this.<br><br>I picked up the phone and started making my own calls.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="ira3zeb">WHY THE WEALTHIEST PEOPLE ON EARTH ARE QUIETLY FLYING TO SHANGHAI</div>

<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="i6iuzyf"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="im9ylgj" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'shila-4.webp' | asset_url }}" id="ir4elzu" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-Oh1MW2aFlH8e">For five months I became a man possessed.<br><br>I cancelled speaking engagements. I read every available paper out of the Shanghai Institute of Biochemistry and Cell Biology, the Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, and the longevity divisions attached to Fudan and ShanghaiTech Universities. I personally reviewed labs, bloodwork, epigenetic clocks, inflammatory panels, and cardiac scans from seventeen patients who had gone through the Shanghai protocol.<br><br>The pattern was no longer deniable.<br><br>The Chinese government has poured a staggering amount of capital into translational longevity science over the last fifteen years — and unlike in the United States, where the field is fragmented across hundreds of competing private startups, Shanghai's major research institutions operate in coordinated clusters. They share data. They share results. They run human trials at a speed that is simply not possible under the current FDA framework.<br><br><b>Bryan Johnson</b> — the man spending two million dollars a year on his Blueprint protocol — has publicly admitted the most advanced peptide work on Earth is being done in Shanghai. <b>Peter Attia</b> has referenced it. So has <b>David Sinclair</b>. They just don't say it on television.<br><br>That is why people who can afford a sixteen-hour flight on a private jet are taking it.<br><br>And what they figured out — the genuinely important part — is that <b>aging is not one process</b>. It is at least twelve distinct biological processes happening at the same time, falling into three categories that must be addressed simultaneously, in sequence, with three different classes of compounds.</div>

<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ivek8a3"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="ivbhnc9" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-1by1"><img src="{{ 'shila-5.webp' | asset_url }}" id="irxowjf" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i0lyhj">Think of your body as a precision machine that has been running on three failing systems at once.<br><br>By age forty, your <b>mitochondria</b> — the energy factories inside every cell — start piling up damaged units faster than your body can recycle them. The process that clears them out, called mitophagy, slows to a crawl. Energy drops. Inflammation rises. Recovery takes weeks instead of days.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="izziuxk">By 50, your <b>NAD+ levels</b> — the molecular fuel that powers more than five hundred enzymatic reactions, including every single DNA-repair pathway you have — are roughly half what they were at twenty. Your sirtuins (the so-called longevity genes) literally cannot function without NAD+. The repair crews are still on payroll. They just have nothing left to work with.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="iwb56zw">By 60, your <b>peptide signaling</b> — the precise messengers that tell your tissues to repair, rebuild, and stay structurally strong — has collapsed. Sleep architecture falls apart. Collagen synthesis crawls. Wounds that healed in three days at thirty now take three weeks. The body forgets how to be young.</div>

<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="imzww3"><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="iywxt7j">
<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="is3wg4d">The longevity research community has known this since the 2013 Lopez-Otin paper <i>The Hallmarks of Aging</i> — the single most-cited paper in the field.<br><br>Every supplement, drug, and protocol marketed to aging Americans over the last thirty years has tried to target <b>one</b> of these hallmarks at a time. NAD+ boosters. Resveratrol. Senolytics. Each one good at one thing. None of them addressing the full picture.<br><br>The Shanghai clusters figured out that you have to hit <b>all three layers</b> — mitochondrial cleanup, NAD+ restoration, peptide signaling — at the same time.<br><br>That is the discovery.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i1dnu3j">WHY EVERYTHING YOU'VE TRIED HAS QUIETLY FAILED</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="why-intro-v19">I have prescribed and reviewed every major longevity intervention available in the United States for the last decade. Let me dismantle the single-compound options you have probably tried — and explain why none of them, on their own, has ever moved the needle for you the way the field promised they would.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="isdenzf"><b>NMN alone.</b><br>Yes, it raises NAD+. But taken without a methyl donor like TMG, it slowly depletes your methylation pathway, drives up homocysteine, and quietly costs you elsewhere. Most NMN brands on Amazon are also under-dosed by 60–70%.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="il8dax5"><b>Resveratrol.</b><br>The Sinclair-era darling. Almost no clinically meaningful effect in humans without active sirtuin substrate (NAD+). It is the spark with no fuel — sold by the millions of bottles to people who never get the second compound.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="it6rayw"><b>Standard testosterone replacement.</b><br>Expensive — $200–400/month — and it addresses exactly one hormone while doing nothing for the underlying mitochondrial, NAD+, and peptide-signaling collapse driving the symptoms in the first place.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="inmbvb9-couples"><b>Concierge longevity clinics.</b><br>$30,000 to $100,000 per year. Marble lobbies, extensive labs, identical underlying protocol. The science they are delivering is real. The markup is the building you are sitting in.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="inmbvb9-natural"><b>"Anti-aging" supplements off Amazon.</b><br>Astragalus. Spermidine. Berberine. Most are under-dosed by an order of magnitude. None of them address all three layers of the aging process. You are paying for the label, not the compound.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="inmbvb9-summary">Every one of these treats a single mechanism while ignoring the other two layers that are still failing.<br><br>That is why nothing has worked.<br><br>That is why your blood markers have not moved.<br><br>That is why the mirror keeps telling the same story.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="ikfy6ba">THE 3-COMPOUND PROTOCOL HIDING IN PLAIN SIGHT</div>

<div data-secondsdelay="" id="i9h53o6" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'shila-6.webp' | asset_url }}" id="il9jsjw" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div>
</div></div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-tGUN1ZootH6a">Remember James?<br><br>Six weeks after I put him on the full three-layer Shanghai protocol, his wife noticed before he did. She told him at breakfast that the texture of his skin had changed. He looked in the mirror three times before he saw it himself.<br><br><b>Day ninety: biological age 34.6. CRP 0.8. VO2 max 41.2. Resting heart rate 58.</b><br><br>His cardiologist — a colleague of mine at Mass General — called me directly and asked me to put his wife on it.<br><br>The protocol is three compounds. Each one targets a different one of the three aging layers. Each one is dosed at the exact level the clinical literature actually demands. And each one is useless without the other two.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i99fgx9"><b>1. AgeAura Pure Urolithin A — the Mitophagy Activator.</b><br>The only compound ever proven in a <i>Nature Metabolism</i> human trial to directly activate mitochondrial recycling. Cleans damaged mitochondria out of your cells the way your body did at thirty. 500 mg clinical dose — not the 100–250 mg cosmetic doses you see on Amazon. This is Layer 1: you cannot rebuild a cell that has not first been cleaned.<br><br><b>2. AgeAura Pure NMN + TMG — the NAD+ Restoration Pair.</b><br>Clinical-dose NMN pre-paired with trimethylglycine — the methyl donor that lets NMN raise NAD+ without taxing your methylation pathway elsewhere. Take NMN alone and you are running a hidden tax. Take them together, the way Shanghai does, and you raise NAD+ cleanly. This is Layer 2: the fuel for every repair you have left.<br><br><b>3. AgeAura Pure Longevity Peptides — the Signaling Layer.</b><br>A pharmaceutical-grade peptide complex sourced from the same manufacturer that supplies several Shanghai clinical programs. Tells your body, at the molecular level, to start behaving the way it did fifteen years ago. Sleep deepens. Recovery accelerates. Skin elasticity returns. Lean tissue rebuilds.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i7dflus">Miss even one layer and you stay stuck.<br><br>That is why every single-compound product on the market has failed you.<br><br>That is why the full protocol works.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-J0TkJtWE0lu0">WORD SPREAD INSIDE THE FIELD</div>

<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ikrobdu"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iy59m94" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'shila-7.webp' | asset_url }}" id="ic97xxa" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-Yev87gre1wCt">After James's panel came back, word got out the way it always does in a tight medical circle. Slowly at first. Then quickly.<br><br>Two cardiologists at Mass General asked me about it. A peptide-therapy MD in New York flew up to review the data. By month four I had patients flying in from Los Angeles, Miami, and Vancouver.<br><br>By month eight I was tracking roughly <b>fourteen hundred patients</b> on the same three-layer protocol — every one of them showing measurable biological-age reduction in their first ninety days.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-MVjB74x9W8ru">AND THEN THE PUSHBACK STARTED</div>

<img title="" target="_self" src="{{ 'shila-8.webp' | asset_url }}" href="" align="center" alt="" width="" height="" onclick="" id="fkt-image-dfd-da1-948" class="fk-image-defaults disable-fk-lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async">

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-tSh4Ox0XjtK7">First it was friendly. A colleague I have known for eighteen years pulled me aside at a longevity-medicine conference and told me, kindly, that what I was describing was <i>"going to make a lot of people uncomfortable."</i><br><br>Then it was less friendly. A polite letter from a supplement industry trade association suggesting I <i>"reconsider how I framed my findings publicly."</i><br><br>Then a regulatory body opened an inquiry — no findings, just an inquiry — that took six months to resolve.<br><br>The reason is obvious.<br><br>American supplement companies make their money selling you one compound at a time, at the lowest possible dose that can legally carry the name on the label. American pharmaceutical companies cannot patent NMN. They cannot patent Urolithin A. They cannot patent naturally occurring peptide sequences. There is nobody with a stock price who is incentivized to put this on the news.</div>

<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="iru1sew"><ul id="i25co5m" class="fk-bullet">
<li id="iznddjl"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iy0vtt8" class="fk-bullet-list-container bullet-list-container"><div data-secondsdelay="" class="fk-bullet-icon-container"><i id="imi45gq" class="icp icp-auto fas fa-circle"></i></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="iqlkjvp">Addresses the <b>ROOT CAUSE</b> of biological aging (all three layers — not one at a time)</div></div></li>
<li id="izicd8g"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iftxdki" class="fk-bullet-list-container bullet-list-container"><div data-secondsdelay="" class="fk-bullet-icon-container"><i id="idvq5rl" class="icp icp-auto fas fa-circle"></i></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="ii3r4uv">Costs less than one month at any concierge longevity clinic</div></div></li>
<li id="ivbhehn"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iuamajf" class="fk-bullet-list-container bullet-list-container"><div data-secondsdelay="" class="fk-bullet-icon-container"><i id="iwdruml" class="icp icp-auto fas fa-circle"></i></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="iurma5d">Delivered to your door — no $200,000 Swiss retreat, no clinic membership fee</div></div></li>
</ul></div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i45ftvo">But here is what the trade associations didn't count on…<br><br>The patients getting their lives back weren't going to stay quiet. They told their spouses. They told their friends. They told their cardiologists.<br><br>The information was moving faster than anyone could shut it down.</div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="itksswy">THE ONLY PROTOCOL THAT DELIVERS ALL THREE LAYERS</div>

<div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="i524twj"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="isyommj" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'shila-9.webp' | asset_url }}" id="iyonet6" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div>

<div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="ihljs5">It is called the <b>AgeAura Pure Protocol</b>.<br><br>Three pharmaceutical-grade compounds. One daily ritual. Clinical doses on every single ingredient. Manufactured to the same specifications as the Shanghai-affiliated clinical programs.<br><br>Available without the flight.</div>

